--TEST--
Inside a `Core\Html::later` slot, `Core\Request` returns the path, a header, a cookie, a query value and a route parameter of the request the slot belongs to, on a normal and on a slotted route. A body read in a slot throws `LogicError`, and the main script still reads the body -- `rule:core-classes/html-later`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Html::later
final class Pages {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/posts/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public static function show(uint $id): void {
        echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => Pages::describe());
    }

    #[Core\Route(path: "/slotted/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, slotted: true)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public static function slotted(uint $id): void {
        echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => Pages::describe());
    }

    #[Core\Route(path: "/save", method: Core\Http\Method::Post)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public static function save(): void {
        // The slot reads the body, which is not allowed.
        echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => {
            try {
                echo Core\Request::body();
            } catch (LogicError $e) {
                echo $e->message, "\n";
            }
        });
        // The main script reads the body and passes the value to the slot.
        tainted string $sent = Core\Request::body();
        echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => { echo $sent; });
    }

    // Each slot above calls this, so it reads the request inside the slot.
    public static function describe(): void {
        var $matched = Core\Request::route();
        echo Core\Request::path(),
             " lang=", Core\Request::header("accept-language") ?? "none",
             " theme=", Core\Request::cookie("theme") ?? "none",
             " page=", Core\Request::queryParameter("page") ?? "none",
             " id=", $matched == null ? "none" : $matched->parameter("id") ?? "none";
    }
}

class Gate implements Core\Router\Gate {
    public function allows(Core\Router\Match $route): bool {
        return true;
    }

    public function refused(Core\Router\Refusal $reason, ?Core\Router\Match $route): void {
        echo "refused";
    }

    public function failed(?Core\Router\Match $route, ?Throwable $error): void {
        echo "failed: ", $error == null ? "" : $error->message;
    }
}

if (Core\Env::context() == Core\Env::Context::Request) {
    Core\Router::dispatch(new Gate());
} else {
    array<string> $headers = ["accept-language" => "de", "cookie" => "theme=dark"];
    echo Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/posts/5?page=2", {headers: $headers})->body(), "\n";
    echo Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/slotted/9?page=4", {headers: $headers})->body(), "\n";
    echo Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Post, "/save", {body: "hello"})->body(), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
/posts/5 lang=de theme=dark page=2 id=5
/slotted/9 lang=de theme=dark page=4 id=9
Core\Request::body() cannot read the request body inside `Core\Html::later`. Read the body in the main script and pass the value to the `later` function
hello
